WEBVTT

00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:05.440
Everyday was like a party.

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:07.990
We hadn't forgotten anything.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.400
We weren't trying to forget anything either.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:13.000
We just wanted some more time.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:16.550
Like children that play ceaselessly as dusk draws near.

00:00:16.830 --> 00:00:19.830
Yet, all the while, the darkness encroaches further.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:55.170
12 Minutes before

00:01:57.810 --> 00:01:59.260
Okay, it's all ready to go.

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:01.180
Are you sure about this?

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:04.070
The bike will keep you completely insulated

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:06.990
from the high voltage running through the corridors.

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:09.020
It also has an independent gyro.

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:11.070
Even if the gravity control is dead, you'll be fine!

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:15.860
We must regain control over the Y Unit in twenty minutes,

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:17.450
or the entire operation will be a complete failure.

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:20.620
All right, let's go, everyone!

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:22.580
35 Minutes before

00:02:23.070 --> 00:02:25.470
Ro'kon shoujyou, ro'kon shoujyou...

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:28.010
A priori usage, total integration, assumed command,

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:29.180
Ro'kon shoujyou...

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:29.990
Thou holy, shall holy, thine holy, holy thee,

00:02:29.990 --> 00:02:31.240
What is she doing?

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:31.610
Thou holy, shall holy, thine holy, holy thee,

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:33.150
Someone saw a ghost.

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:33.190
holy, ho-ho, hoo-li holee, hoddle-ho!

00:02:33.190 --> 00:02:34.070
A ghost?

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:35.330
holy, ho-ho, hoo-li holee, hoddle-ho!

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:36.880
8 Minutes before

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:40.800
Nii-san... How? I thought you were dead.

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:42.760
?? Minutes before
~Memories Mahjong~

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:50.940
Oh, mahjong...

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:52.360
Whose past is that?

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:11.540
Two Gekigan type units approaching.

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:13.840
Requesting all Aestivalis launch to intercept.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.800
54 Minutes before
~Battle at the Darkside of the Moon~

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:19.360
Commander Tsukiomi, we were supposed to rendezvous with the lunar surface forces by now.

00:03:19.850 --> 00:03:23.140
We have been led to an encounter with that battleship by the benevolent Gekiganger!

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:25.860
Let the unmanned forces handle the lunar surface.

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:28.060
We will sink this ship here and now.

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:28.990
Understood.

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:31.450
Here they come!

00:03:41.690 --> 00:03:42.320
Damn!

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:48.330
The Gekigan type units are compromising our distortion field.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:51.750
It seems that our field can only delay the enemy's encroachment,

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:53.500
ever since the Gekigan types have started appearing.

00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:56.220
Stop calling them "Gekigan types"!

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:07.240
Gotcha!

00:04:09.720 --> 00:04:12.690
Got rhythm? Got cha-cha?

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:18.650
Enemy vessel has accelerated.

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:20.570
To fire their boson cannon?

00:04:20.980 --> 00:04:22.130
Do we want to retreat?

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:24.490
We know that they can't touch us from long range.

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:28.630
If we change heading now, we won't reach the designated point in time.

00:04:29.380 --> 00:04:30.500
The phase transition cannon...

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:31.920
Keep the Nadesico advancing toward the target as planned.

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:33.330
I'll smash this ship!

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.290
80 minutes before
~Strategy Room~

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:38.710
I'll begin the briefing for this operation.

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:41.940
Currently, the Second Fleet is on the final offensive

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:44.050
on the dark side of the Moon, employing massive numbers of

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:46.430
lunar surface frames and recently-completed vessels.

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:50.280
We will lure the formidable Jovian boson-cannon equipped vessels

00:04:50.280 --> 00:04:52.890
and their manned robot forces to this point.

00:04:53.420 --> 00:04:55.660
Our fields are useless against the boson cannon.

00:04:55.660 --> 00:04:57.320
Why are we making a bad situation worse?

00:04:57.700 --> 00:04:59.030
We will use the phase transition cannon.

00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:00.150
Phase transition cannon?

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:02.860
Right! We use the Y Unit's onboard systems.

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:04.240
The three phase transition engines...

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:05.150
Hey!

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:09.760
We forcibly phase transition a point in space using the Y Unit.

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:12.660
No field protection scheme will be effective against this.

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:14.460
With the phase transition cannon,

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:16.440
we can eliminate all manned vessels near the Moon.

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:18.430
The Moon will be all ours again.

00:05:18.430 --> 00:05:21.850
Put bluntly, this operation's success hinges on the Nadesico.

00:05:21.850 --> 00:05:26.260
The problem is arriving at the firing coordinates on time.

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:30.050
We must reach that point in eighty minutes.

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:32.920
Tenkawa-kun...

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:35.350
Artificial boson jumping?

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:39.280
It's possible to create a jump field using the CCs.

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:39.820
The rest hinges on...

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:42.530
Whether or not a regular person can withstand the jumping, right?

00:05:43.170 --> 00:05:45.260
I would like to participate in this experiment as well.

00:05:45.260 --> 00:05:45.810
You too?

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:47.490
Would you mind?

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:49.450
45 Minutes before

00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:56.620
The jump field is stable.

00:05:56.870 --> 00:05:57.290
You can jump now.

00:05:57.970 --> 00:05:59.910
Chronological linearity can be compromised in jumping

00:05:59.910 --> 00:06:02.590
because the field becomes unstable. So...

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:05.180
Akito, if you have second thoughts, tell us now!

00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:06.180
Are you feeling all right?

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:07.790
Akito, don't push it!

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:11.060
Enemy vessels rapidly approaching. Phase transition activity detected.

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:12.450
Boson cannon, readying to fire.

00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:12.850
I'm doing it!

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:14.540
Visualize!

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:15.880
Your target is the enemy battleship!

00:06:24.710 --> 00:06:26.270
There! Fire!

00:06:39.610 --> 00:06:43.230
Damn those evil Earthlings! Our precious leap cannon is lost!

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:46.050
Ready the Daimajin! I will attack them directly!

00:06:46.610 --> 00:06:48.810
Wait, Genichiro. Pull back for now!

00:06:48.810 --> 00:06:50.350
Tsukumo? But I can't...

00:06:50.350 --> 00:06:51.220
I said, pull back!

00:06:51.390 --> 00:06:53.180
?? Minutes before
~Memories Mahjong~

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:56.600
Doesn't it seem that Akito has changed all of a sudden?

00:06:57.310 --> 00:07:01.400
His newfound ability to boson jump successfully probably has the most to do with it.

00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:05.390
Every child wants to be a hero while they're small,

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:08.950
but that desire turns into a burden as you grow older.

00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:13.020
Tenkawa Akito-kun's disdain for the IFS connector,

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:15.610
and his insistence that he is actually a cook

00:07:15.610 --> 00:07:19.140
even while he regularly pilots the Aestivalis, are examples of this.

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:20.880
Stop peeking into my past without my permission!

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:22.470
What can I do about it?

00:07:22.470 --> 00:07:24.650
It looks like this is just the place for that.

00:07:24.930 --> 00:07:25.550
Here we go.

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:33.000
But you're very different now, Tenkawa-kun.

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:37.140
Being the first to be able to make it through organic boson jumping

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:38.940
made you a real hero for both Earth and Mars.

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:40.640
A hero?

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:42.690
Well, you have gotten a lot more resilient recently.

00:07:43.240 --> 00:07:46.120
I could never make it as a hero.

00:07:46.390 --> 00:07:47.410
That's what I thought.

00:07:48.020 --> 00:07:49.630
Well, it isn't only me.

00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:54.240
In a real war, no single person can be a real hero.

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:57.050
If you try, you'll end up like Gai.

00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:03.710
But I guess I have do this right, since I'm the one that can do it.

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:06.510
Then how things are now is all right.

00:08:07.210 --> 00:08:09.100
Fighting against the enemy with your life at stake

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:11.260
is the Gekiganger life that Akito wanted, right?

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:13.170
Except the enemy are humans.

00:08:13.350 --> 00:08:15.140
30 Minutes before
~Abnormal Event~

00:08:20.170 --> 00:08:20.600
Here, too?

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:23.760
No way! We can't get through with this here.

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:23.980
Damn!

00:08:27.910 --> 00:08:30.070
Something's wrong with the connection to the Y Unit.

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:34.360
To be specific, Y Unit's weapons control computer, Sarutahiko,

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:36.130
is not responding to my commands.

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:38.750
All software level diagnostics have been blocked.

00:08:39.170 --> 00:08:41.780
Is this a hardware issue? What about the mechanics?

00:08:41.780 --> 00:08:43.170
Screw this, damn it!

00:08:43.490 --> 00:08:47.030
All passageways leading to the Y Unit from the Nadesico

00:08:47.030 --> 00:08:48.250
have high voltage flowing through them,

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:50.170
or their gravitational controls are all dead.

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:53.590
It's as if the Y Unit doesn't want to let anyone in!

00:08:54.020 --> 00:08:54.830
Will it be possible to fire

00:08:54.830 --> 00:08:57.010
the phase transition cannon in thirty minutes?

00:08:57.420 --> 00:09:01.060
It's impossible with the Y Unit not responding to our commands.

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:04.440
Could the lesson be, "Don't be greedy and try to bag them all at once"?

00:09:04.840 --> 00:09:06.590
Then somebody has to actually go to the Y Unit,

00:09:06.590 --> 00:09:08.480
and get it operational again.

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:10.850
But our pilots are not doing too well.

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:12.450
Is something wrong?

00:09:12.700 --> 00:09:14.150
They claim to be seeing ghosts.

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:16.110
34 Minutes before
~Those, who saw ghosts~

00:09:21.030 --> 00:09:22.500
Yamada-san?

00:09:22.810 --> 00:09:24.720
What's up, Ruri-Ruri?

00:09:25.180 --> 00:09:26.130
Yamada-san?

00:09:26.430 --> 00:09:28.960
There are others there too. Who are they?

00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:37.260
18 Minutes before
~Y Unit~

00:09:39.110 --> 00:09:42.450
Never thought I'd be riding around the Nadesico on a bicycle!

00:09:42.450 --> 00:09:44.100
Oh yeah, let's go!

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:47.020
My, aren't you pumped up, Tenkawa-kun.

00:09:47.510 --> 00:09:51.940
Hey, why don't we race each other, to see who can get to Sarutahiko first?

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:53.860
Hey, I like that. Why not?

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:55.370
And, and, how about this?

00:09:55.660 --> 00:09:57.530
The one who makes it there first gets something from the losers.

00:09:57.900 --> 00:09:59.510
Hey, no problem!

00:10:00.020 --> 00:10:01.700
You must be after my body.

00:10:02.070 --> 00:10:03.620
If I win, I get to have the Captain.

00:10:04.050 --> 00:10:05.400
Hey, wait just a second.

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:07.880
She's not mine to give out anyway!

00:10:07.880 --> 00:10:08.290
Hey!

00:10:10.820 --> 00:10:12.920
Akatsuki-kun sure has strange tastes.

00:10:13.660 --> 00:10:15.130
He sure does.

00:10:15.270 --> 00:10:17.340
Just listen to them! How inappropriate!

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:19.050
There you go, getting all jealous.

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:22.310
Why should I be?! He's just doing that to rattle Akito's cage!

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:24.110
Oh, whatever.

00:10:24.110 --> 00:10:26.230
But is it me or have their personalities all changed?

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:30.140
Well, Akito does seem to be a lot more energetic than usual.

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:32.110
15 Minutes before

00:10:32.450 --> 00:10:35.530
Are sure about this? Let's forget it, okay?

00:10:35.800 --> 00:10:37.950
Well... ah...

00:10:40.190 --> 00:10:41.700
I... I...

00:10:46.010 --> 00:10:48.970
Come on, get on your bicycles! We're going in!

00:10:48.970 --> 00:10:54.470
I... I... I just want something to shoot!

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:01.760
40 Minutes before
~Jovian Yuujin's Main Force~

00:11:07.790 --> 00:11:09.600
Jovian Yuujin Forces' Mother Ship Kagurazuki

00:11:10.330 --> 00:11:12.520
Our goal is to achieve peace in the universe.

00:11:12.740 --> 00:11:15.790
Exactly. That is why we fight.

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:19.100
Then it is imperative we consider a negotiated peace!

00:11:20.490 --> 00:11:22.730
Of course, first we must have Earth agree

00:11:22.730 --> 00:11:24.830
to make a full apology for their past injustices.

00:11:25.100 --> 00:11:25.540
Eventually,

00:11:26.230 --> 00:11:29.660
the ancient phase transition core fabrication plant will break down.

00:11:29.990 --> 00:11:32.220
Our excavations on Mars are not producing the desired results.

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:34.210
Is it really possible?

00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:36.120
I have a plan.

00:11:38.270 --> 00:11:39.510
Now! Let's...

00:11:39.730 --> 00:11:40.820
Gekiga-in!

00:11:54.290 --> 00:11:57.450
Tsukumo! Why did you pull me out of that fight?!

00:11:58.290 --> 00:11:59.550
Oh, about that...

00:12:00.730 --> 00:12:01.570
Onii-chan!

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:02.660
Yukina?!

00:12:03.050 --> 00:12:04.760
Wha... What are you doing here?

00:12:06.850 --> 00:12:08.040
I heard all about it, Onii-chan!

00:12:09.960 --> 00:12:10.710
Nanako-san!

00:12:11.370 --> 00:12:12.290
Are you all right?

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:15.480
It was my mackerel sushi that put them out of action.

00:12:15.480 --> 00:12:16.750
I've got to pull through.

00:12:20.680 --> 00:12:21.640
Whoa!

00:12:22.250 --> 00:12:23.040
Onii-chan!

00:12:24.090 --> 00:12:25.660
Yukina, that's "onii-sama, Tsukumo."

00:12:25.660 --> 00:12:27.800
You'll appreciate Gekiganger as you get older...

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:28.770
I hate manga!

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:31.440
But what's this about peace negotiations with the Earthlings?

00:12:32.080 --> 00:12:33.190
Is this true, Tsukumo?

00:12:33.760 --> 00:12:34.610
Well, actually, I'm...

00:12:35.210 --> 00:12:36.550
What's the meaning of this?!

00:12:36.550 --> 00:12:38.030
Are you going to forgive those brutes?

00:12:38.460 --> 00:12:41.720
We need to find a new path toward peace!

00:12:41.720 --> 00:12:42.360
That's all bull!

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:47.090
Onii-chan has been deceived by an Earth woman!

00:12:51.780 --> 00:12:53.580
You disgust me, onii-chan!

00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:56.040
?? Minutes before
~Where is here?~

00:12:56.470 --> 00:12:59.710
It looks like our memories have all become interconnected.

00:13:00.110 --> 00:13:02.380
This isn't a dream?

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:05.150
If it was a dream, we wouldn't see each other's past memories.

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:08.580
Well, so you were a bed wetter until you were ten?

00:13:09.310 --> 00:13:11.030
But I'm not one anymore!

00:13:12.020 --> 00:13:12.390
Baka.

00:13:12.610 --> 00:13:17.320
So if our personalities are here, what's going on with our bodies?

00:13:17.490 --> 00:13:20.160
They're being driven by our other personalities,

00:13:20.160 --> 00:13:21.610
the personalities usually repressed within ourselves.

00:13:21.780 --> 00:13:23.570
10 Minutes before
~Those, who rushed in and were suspressed~

00:13:27.310 --> 00:13:29.080
That's it. The hatch to the Y Unit!

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:33.160
Just you wait! You stubborn computer!

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:35.120
43 Minutes before

00:13:35.390 --> 00:13:37.540
Aestivalis has appeared right in front of the enemy flagship.

00:13:38.020 --> 00:13:40.280
Tenkawa-san has successfully boson jumped.

00:13:40.280 --> 00:13:41.200
Wow.

00:13:42.020 --> 00:13:43.970
All right, Erina-kun. Now it's my turn!

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:45.170
Are you sure?

00:13:45.170 --> 00:13:48.310
Why not? I can handle this just fine!

00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:53.900
Let's go!

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:08.070
What is it?

00:14:08.740 --> 00:14:10.200
I aborted the jump from here.

00:14:10.470 --> 00:14:11.830
You cannot make it!

00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:12.500
Why?

00:14:12.980 --> 00:14:15.040
Take a look at yourself!

00:14:18.510 --> 00:14:20.900
Damn it! I can't jump?

00:14:21.400 --> 00:14:22.230
Nii-san...

00:14:22.820 --> 00:14:24.050
An older brother much older than you,

00:14:24.550 --> 00:14:26.210
so he was being groomed as the successor.

00:14:27.390 --> 00:14:28.970
So what?

00:14:29.230 --> 00:14:30.200
How did he die?

00:14:30.200 --> 00:14:31.640
An accident on the Mars route.

00:14:31.980 --> 00:14:35.060
Do you still wish that your brother was alive?

00:14:35.540 --> 00:14:36.850
I said none of this matters anymore!

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:38.810
8 minutes before
~Those stood still~

00:14:41.930 --> 00:14:43.820
Why? Why are you here?

00:14:44.210 --> 00:14:47.740
Nii-san... How? I thought you were dead.

00:14:55.310 --> 00:14:55.980
Gai...

00:14:57.470 --> 00:14:59.920
What? Why are those three just standing there?!

00:15:00.250 --> 00:15:03.690
Hello, Akito-san? Izumi-san? Akatsuki-san?

00:15:03.690 --> 00:15:05.660
What's the matter? Anyone?
Do they see something strange?

00:15:05.660 --> 00:15:05.810
Maybe.

00:15:05.810 --> 00:15:07.230
Hello? Hello?

00:15:07.230 --> 00:15:08.500
What about the Aoi and Subaru party?

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:12.400
Oh, I'm going to blast away!

00:15:12.400 --> 00:15:14.740
Somebody help me!

00:15:15.900 --> 00:15:18.110
So, what exactly is happening here?

00:15:18.110 --> 00:15:20.050
The personalities of all our pilots have changed.

00:15:20.050 --> 00:15:21.560
They're acting very peculiar.

00:15:21.850 --> 00:15:23.980
Inez-san isn't showing up to give us her explanation either.

00:15:28.890 --> 00:15:31.260
Gai, you died.

00:15:38.730 --> 00:15:41.170
Gai, are you trying to stop us?

00:15:42.470 --> 00:15:44.000
Is there something you want to tell me, Gai?

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:46.210
The dead won't say anything.

00:15:47.480 --> 00:15:49.340
There are no such things as ghosts in this world.

00:15:49.710 --> 00:15:51.810
You yourselves have created them.

00:15:51.810 --> 00:15:54.070
When our memories and personalities were interconnected,

00:15:54.070 --> 00:15:56.010
what was suppressed has come back to life.

00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:58.600
You are being held back by none other then yourself.

00:15:58.770 --> 00:16:00.560
5 Minutes before
~Those encountered~

00:16:00.880 --> 00:16:03.180
When will you stop pulling me back?

00:16:04.890 --> 00:16:06.480
Just get away from me!

00:16:10.060 --> 00:16:12.160
I'm not afraid anymore.

00:16:12.600 --> 00:16:14.970
Hey, Izumi, who is this man?

00:16:15.470 --> 00:16:17.440
Didn't you have two fiancés?

00:16:17.820 --> 00:16:22.200
But didn't both of them die?

00:16:22.740 --> 00:16:25.110
One lost to disease, the other to an accident.

00:16:25.550 --> 00:16:27.610
I'm a woman that invites misfortune.

00:16:27.610 --> 00:16:29.010
Guess I'm not really popular like that.

00:16:29.710 --> 00:16:32.480
I know. You've come to take me with you.

00:16:33.080 --> 00:16:35.190
It's all right. I'm so tired.

00:16:35.670 --> 00:16:37.140
I can't love anyone again, anyway.

00:16:43.520 --> 00:16:46.610
You... You're not here to take me?

00:16:47.310 --> 00:16:49.270
Please? Please!

00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:51.340
For these two, it wasn't the deaths themselves,

00:16:51.340 --> 00:16:53.430
but rather their strong attachment to their lost loved ones.

00:16:53.430 --> 00:16:55.280
That's why they can't move on.

00:16:56.210 --> 00:16:57.950
So what about you, Akito-kun?

00:16:58.540 --> 00:17:01.200
You never wanted to come to terms with the death of Yamada Jiro,

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:03.990
because that would mean accepting one's own fear of death.

00:17:04.370 --> 00:17:06.120
I am not afraid! Not of dying!

00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:06.810
3 Minutes before

00:17:06.810 --> 00:17:09.090
Oh, really? And?

00:17:11.360 --> 00:17:13.820
I get scared. That's why I fight.

00:17:14.450 --> 00:17:16.480
Because if I don't fight, we're all going to die.

00:17:16.900 --> 00:17:19.520
Me, my friends, and all the people of Earth.

00:17:20.710 --> 00:17:22.940
There you go, all high and mighty on your horse.

00:17:23.440 --> 00:17:25.690
Haven't we moved up in the ranks, Tenkawa Akito!

00:17:25.690 --> 00:17:26.390
I...

00:17:32.330 --> 00:17:34.160
The first day I rode a bicycle.

00:17:35.210 --> 00:17:37.270
The first day I rode through the meadows.

00:17:39.100 --> 00:17:41.200
I get it! There are no reasons!

00:17:41.880 --> 00:17:44.220
I understand. I understand now, Gai!

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:46.370
3 Minutes before
~Enemy's Main Forces~

00:17:49.770 --> 00:17:52.220
We have the large enemy fleet behind the Moon in our sights.

00:17:52.650 --> 00:17:53.630
Is the Y Unit back online yet?

00:17:53.800 --> 00:17:55.590
1 Minute before

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:12.070
Bastard!

00:18:12.310 --> 00:18:14.150
Operation Time
~Phase Transition Cannon~

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:16.190
Ready the phase transition cannon.

00:18:16.190 --> 00:18:17.510
Expanding Y Unit.

00:18:18.050 --> 00:18:20.600
Y-Unit phase transition engines raise power output to maximum load.

00:18:20.600 --> 00:18:21.660
Maximum power.

00:18:23.640 --> 00:18:25.410
Locked on to enemy fleet coordinates.

00:18:25.770 --> 00:18:26.600
Fire!

00:18:31.340 --> 00:18:33.000
All hands abandon ship! All hands...

00:18:33.540 --> 00:18:35.990
It destroys space itself.

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:38.480
Unbelievable firepower...

00:18:38.900 --> 00:18:41.140
We can't use a weapon this powerful.

00:18:41.620 --> 00:18:43.850
It's certainly the last word.

00:18:47.430 --> 00:18:49.230
15 Minutes later
~Inez-sensei's Explanation~

00:18:49.520 --> 00:18:52.150
The nanomachines create an auxiliary brain near the brain itself.

00:18:52.990 --> 00:18:56.420
Memories, converted into electronic data are stored there as well.

00:18:56.740 --> 00:18:58.720
The hermit crab specializes in hacking electronic data,

00:18:58.720 --> 00:19:01.160
so that must have appeared as a form of computer memory.

00:19:01.500 --> 00:19:04.340
So, how did our minds all get stuck talking to each other?

00:19:04.660 --> 00:19:05.620
That's the result of our communicators.

00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:09.570
Our data centers are all linked to each other through our communicators.

00:19:09.910 --> 00:19:12.620
The hermit crab perceived them to be part of a network.

00:19:12.620 --> 00:19:14.290
By attempting to compromise the entire network,

00:19:14.290 --> 00:19:15.700
the hermit crab brought about the linking of all our consciousness.

00:19:16.240 --> 00:19:20.190
But what kind of data was the enemy after from the Nadesico?

00:19:20.190 --> 00:19:20.900
Unknown.

00:19:21.490 --> 00:19:24.720
Inez-san and I haven't gone through nanomachine treatment.

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:25.390
So it seems strange that...

00:19:25.390 --> 00:19:26.350
Unknown also.

00:19:26.640 --> 00:19:28.270
Well, isn't that rare?

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:31.650
What? You've already sent a peace emissary?

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:33.920
Yes, following your recommendations,

00:19:33.920 --> 00:19:36.180
I have sent an emissary to this Nadesico you mentioned.

00:19:36.180 --> 00:19:37.580
I made no such recommendation!

00:19:37.830 --> 00:19:39.070
Who did you send to the Nadesico?

00:19:40.780 --> 00:19:42.770
Just what the plot calls for, of course, Tsukumo.

00:19:44.830 --> 00:19:46.620
How dare she deceive onii-chan?!

00:19:47.420 --> 00:19:49.500
Earth woman, just you wait!

00:19:50.060 --> 00:19:52.220
You won't cooperate in the experiments any more? Why?

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:54.700
You're the only one that can jump!

00:19:54.700 --> 00:19:56.520
Who will protect the Nadesico?

00:19:57.520 --> 00:19:59.770
It's just like how it is in your favorite, Gekiganger.

00:19:59.770 --> 00:20:02.090
You fight the enemy to protect the blue Earth.

00:20:02.880 --> 00:20:05.410
But is that really right?

00:20:05.710 --> 00:20:08.980
Fighting to protect something is ordinary, but...

00:20:09.590 --> 00:20:10.640
You're still killing people.

00:20:12.170 --> 00:20:13.900
You need a reason to fight.

00:20:14.380 --> 00:20:15.730
Is that what a hero is about?

00:20:15.900 --> 00:20:18.690
?? Minutes later
~The "Meadows" We Once Ran Across~

00:20:19.090 --> 00:20:22.200
That's weird. What's Ai-chan doing here?

00:20:22.630 --> 00:20:25.370
Oh! Here we go. Akito's and my memory!

00:20:27.210 --> 00:20:27.690
See!

00:21:43.840 --> 00:21:45.840
Don't fool around with me, my dear.

00:21:45.840 --> 00:21:47.320
Just listen to you go, Haruka!

00:21:47.370 --> 00:21:49.890
I'm not fooling around, my sweet.

00:21:49.890 --> 00:21:51.040
Quit clowning around, Tsukumo!

00:21:51.070 --> 00:21:54.160
Look at you go at it, with a cool face like that.

00:21:54.160 --> 00:21:55.120
Do what? What?!

00:21:55.190 --> 00:21:57.130
Oh, I'm nothing compared to you, my dear.

00:21:57.130 --> 00:21:58.660
Well, is that so?

00:21:59.200 --> 00:22:03.130
Living apart, the love between us, it burns ever more brightly...

00:22:03.750 --> 00:22:07.380
Well, sorry for interrupting, this is next episode preview.

00:22:07.380 --> 00:22:09.340
Next episode "Protect the Visitor?"

00:22:09.600 --> 00:22:10.600
Please, enjoy it!
